# JNLisp Language Playground

A little workbook for playing with the features of my literate Lisp-based
Domain Specific Language (DSL) for interacting with my CFD library, but
it can also do lots of cool things!  It is reasonably complete with most
Lisps aside from any quoting/macro features (so maybe it's actually not
that complete).  But, for basic algorithms and maths-y stuff it's pretty
convenient.  Here are some examples:

## Core data types

Some errors that should show up as syntax errors

j(define (jed n y) (* n (* 5 y)))

j(define (hello y) [5 6 7)

j(define name "hello)
